<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42227" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Saetăbis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēt-</span></b> ), is, f.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of</i>
			Hispania Tarraconensis, <i>celebrated for its flax</i>
			(now <i>Jativa</i>), <i><span class="en">Plin. 19, 1,
				2, § 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 3, 374</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 2,
			6</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Saetăbĭtāni</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēt-</span></b> ),
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Sœtabis</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 3,
				4, § 25</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Saetăbus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sēt-</span></b> ),
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Sœtabis</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sudaria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					12, 14</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
